        "The chapter discusses US state EMS law, consent, confidentiality, medical direction, and professional responsibilities. The applicable jurisdiction, agency, and medical director determine actual authority. A textbook explains principles but does not create permission to act. Legal details can differ by place and change over time, so this lesson preserves the course's distinctions without presenting its examples as universal law.",
