        "The course says to document assessment, evidence of capacity, recommended care or transport, the risks explained, patient statements, consultation, and the refusal itself. Obtain the appropriate signatures or document refusal to sign according to procedure, and notify medical direction as required. A form does not replace the discussion and does not remove the need for a PCR.",
        "Write enough that someone who was not present can understand what the patient declined and on what basis the decision was accepted. Do not reduce a complex encounter to 'refused, signed.' Record relevant advice and the path back to care if the patient changes their mind or worsens."
